I've independently verified the changes and confirmed the analysis. `runCompletion` is always invoked with a message array ending in a user turn (KeatingProvider.tsx line 290 appends the user message; line 312 slices to `userIndex + 1`). Given the alternating user/assistant sequence, once a conversation exceeds 40 non-empty messages, `.slice(-40)` begins on an assistant turn. Typecheck and all 43 tests pass. Both prior agents converged on the same single substantive defect, which my inspection corroborates.

{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P2] Truncated provider history can start on an assistant turn, breaking Anthropic/Gemini",
      "body": "In `mobile/src/lib/provider-client.ts`, `recentMessages()` returns a raw `.slice(-MAX_HISTORY_MESSAGES)` (40) of the non-empty transcript. `runCompletion` in `KeatingProvider.tsx` always passes a message list ending on a `user` turn, so once a conversation exceeds 40 non-empty messages the sliced window begins with an `assistant` message (e.g. 20 completed exchanges plus the next user prompt). That window is sent verbatim to Anthropic's `/messages`, which rejects requests whose first message is not a `user` turn, and Gemini's `contents` has the same alternation expectation; the OpenAI-compatible path is unaffected because it prepends a `system` message. The result is that long Anthropic/Google sessions (>40 turns) start failing until enough history is trimmed. Consider dropping a leading assistant message after slicing so the window always begins on a user turn.",
      "confidence_score": 0.82,
      "priority": 2,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/home/diogenes/Projects/keating/mobile/src/lib/provider-client.ts",
        "line_range": {"start": 32, "end": 35}
      }
    }
  ],
  "overall_correctness": "patch is incorrect",
  "overall_explanation": "The mobile app typechecks, all 43 tests pass, and gitignore/version-sync/dependency wiring is sound, but the provider history truncation introduces a real long-session failure mode for Anthropic (and likely Gemini) users whose conversations exceed 40 non-empty messages, so the patch is not fully free of bugs.",
  "overall_confidence_score": 0.78
}

